# KISS

If someone has to think hard to understand the code, simplify it.

- Prefer clear names and short functions over clever one-liners.
- No nested ternaries in JSX — use flat conditionals or small components.
- Don't optimize until you have a measured problem.
- Don't add libraries for problems solvable in a few lines of existing stack.
- Don't invent abstractions for a single use site.
- Match existing patterns in this repo before introducing new ones.

```tsx
// ❌ nested ternary
{a ? (b ? <A /> : <B />) : <C />}

// ✅ flat
{a && b && <A />}
{a && !b && <B />}
{!a && <C />}
```
